@startuml resolve-turn-activity
' SPEC: _spec/packages/starchess-core/resolve-turn-activity.puml
' purpose: resolveTurn control flow — how one classical plan is classified into a
' bucket, and what each phase then does with those buckets.
' covers: packages/starchess-core/src/resolve/resolve-turn.ts
' covers: packages/starchess-core/src/__tests__/rook/**
' see also: _spec/packages/starchess-core/gas-phase-vacancy.puml
!include ../../themes/proveo.puml

skinparam defaultTextAlignment left

title StarChess Core · ""resolveTurn"" — plan classification and phase run

start
:Read ""placement"" once (""start"" map), clamp ""ccLives"",\ncollect plans white-then-black (""plansOf"");
:Buckets for this pass:\n""attacks"" · ""moveCollisions"" · ""occupy"" · ""quiets""\n""pathRevealPending"" · ""deadSquares"";

partition "Classify — an ordered rule list, first match wins" {
  :build ""PlanContext"" once: actor · target · ""visible0"" · ""leaps"" ·\nsieged flags · a **memoised** ""scanRay"";
  :walk ""RULES"" — each returns a ""PlanOutcome"" or ""null"" (pass);
  :""applyOutcome"" is the **only** writer into the phase buckets;

  note right
    **The list is the precedence.** Reordering ""RULES"" is a one-line diff;
    that ordering used to be implicit in ~200 lines of control flow.

    | # | rule | claims when |
    | 1 | ""jumpImmunity"" | enemy queen listed in ""ignoreAttacksOn"" — a jumping BattleShip is untouchable this turn |
    | 2 | ""marineFrontStep"" | marine, same file: the whole path is walked and the **first occupant blocks** — quiet step onto the last empty square, or stay put. Never a victim, never a discovery, whatever the fog says; a truncated step drops its ""promotion"" |
    | 3 | ""enemyKingSquare"" | enemy king on ""to"" — never arms deferred HP (checks are implicit at turn open). A non-king enemy on the ray is taken: visible ⇒ phase-1 capture, still fogged ⇒ move collision, lights mid-walk ⇒ phase-3 approach. An ally, a king, or a clear ray fizzles — the slider never occupies the king |
    | 4 | ""allyOccupied"" | own unit on ""to"" |
    | 5 | ""marineDiagonalEmpty"" | marine diagonal onto an empty tile — capture-only, unless a **visible** hostile mine is the target |
    | 6 | ""midPathPrecedence"" | slider aimed at an enemy: a unit met **on the ray** always beats the further target (""Re1→e8"" with ""pe7"" + ""re8"" takes the pawn). Ally ⇒ quiet truncate; a **king** passes to rule 9 |
    | 7 | ""targetOnDestination"" | enemy on ""to"" — visible ⇒ phase-1 attack · lights mid-walk ⇒ phase-3 approach · still fogged ⇒ move collision (sieged rooks fizzle: they never relocate, so they never contact a fogged square) |
    | 8 | ""minedEmptyDestination"" | empty ""to"" with a hostile mine — ""attacksOwnDest"" + visible + reachable ⇒ attack-clear (a sieged tank fires without vacating), else quiet so phase 2 takes the mover. ""attacksOwnDest"" now admits the **king**: it shoots the tile and moves in, so "walking over" a mine is attack/move (""mine-contact.puml""), and a king always sees its own destination so it never falls through to the quiet path |
    | 9 | ""slideIntoFog"" | slider into an empty ""to"" — first enemy that is (or becomes) visible on the ray. A king only chips via fog discovery, otherwise the slide stops short |
    | 10 | ""siegedEmptyShelling"" | sieged rook, empty ""to"" on the cross, clear ray, visible — victimless ""shelling"" at ""to"" (no death, no occupy, never relocates). Ally/king contact holds fire (drop); fogged stays quiet (never relocates) |
    | 11 | ""quietFallthrough"" | nothing claimed it |
  end note

  note right
    **Outcomes, not mutations.** A rule returns ""drop"" · ""quiet"" · ""occupy"" ·
    ""capture(fogged?)"" · ""mineClear"" · ""shelling"" · ""approach"" — and ""applyOutcome"" owns
    every bucket write. One consequence is structural rather than remembered:
    a **fogged** capture can only reach ""moveCollisions"" and a visible one only
    ""attacks"", because a single ""fogged"" flag picks the list. Dual-listing is
    no longer expressible.

    **Buckets carry the plan, not a copy of three fields.** Every bucket write
    spreads the plan and overrides ""to"" — a rebuilt ""{color, from, to}"" literal
    silently drops ""promotion"", which is how a last-rank **capture** used to
    land a marine on rank 8 and leave it a marine while the quiet push (pushed
    by reference) promoted fine. Rule 2's truncated step is the one deliberate
    drop, and it drops the whole step, not just the choice.

    ""pathRevealSteps"" does not test vision from ""from"", so a target already
    lit can still report steps > 0. Path discovery therefore needs **fogged at
    start** *and* lit while walking — otherwise a visible target would wrongly
    defer to a phase-3 approach.
  end note

  note right
    A fogged capture or approach whose
    START-board victim departs via its
    own queued plan never books the
    kill. The plan parks on "delayed".
  end note
}

partition "Phase 1 — attack" {
  :remove ""deadSquares"" → **afterAttack** snapshot;
}

partition "Phase 2 — move (""moveWave"": plan every landing, then time them)" {
  :skip movers that died in phase 1, and sieged rooks (never relocate);
  :""planLanding"" — every mover plans against the **same** pre-wave board,
so plan order (white first) can never decide an outcome. Quiet slides
truncate on the first **stationary** blocker — enemy blocker is captured,
ally / king blocker stops the slide one square short;
  :two opposite-colour landings → ""moverContact(timedMover(a), timedMover(b))""
(""move-timing.puml"": Hoverbike 1 tick / square, everything else 2,
leapers hold only their landing, sliders every ray square,
a mover a mine takes on landing holds nothing afterwards);
  if (contact at X?) then (yes)
    if (a Command Center in the pair?) then (yes)
      :CC reached X **first** → CC lands, the other stops one ray
square short (a leaper stays home) · CC arrived on or after the
other → CC **takes** it (""moveCollisions"" capture, occupies,
clears the mine on X) · CC vs CC → neither moves;
    else (no)
      :**both die on X**, mines untouched, no cue — whether the other
was parked there, arrived the same tick, or they passed head-on
mid-edge (reported on the lower-named square);
    endif
  else (no)
    :``land`` each mover as planned;
  endif
  :``land``: destination still held by an enemy → capture + occupy, **unless**\nanother mover already landed there (""destinationsWritten"", phase 3 only)\n→ **both die**, tile empty, no cue;
  :""mineContact"" over ""[extraStepFrom?, …pathContactSquares, dest]""
(mode **walk**) — one ordered scan answers chase **and** walk-over.
A plan carrying ""extraStepTo"" **stands down**: its landing is one hop
further, so the phase-4 arrival owns the contact list
(""mine-contact.puml"" · one walk per marine);
  :land the mover, stamp ""destinationsWritten"", defer promotion;
  :""detonated"" → blast at the landing tile, mover dies, no promotion\nand no occupy left behind; ""chaseFrom"" set when the mine was woken\nmid-path (the first mine touched wins);
  :→ **afterMove** snapshot;
}

partition "Phase 3 — fog approaches" {
  :fizzle gates (in order): sieged origin · origin re-occupied by a\nphase-2 mover · attacker no longer on ""pathRevealFrom"" ·\n""to"" no longer holds the exact discovered victim;
  :fired → ""pathRevealAttacks"" (the only mid-resolve king HP chip);
  :the approach **walked** its ray — ""mineContact"" over that walk takes\nthe mover on its landing tile → ""pathRevealMineTriggers"".\nThe shot already fired, so capture / HP chip stand;
}

partition "Delayed landings — fogged aims whose victim vacated" {
  :sync ""mines"" to the phase-3 epoch, order the pair so a plan\nlanding on the other's origin runs second (mutual swap lands both);
  :skip fired approaches (""firedFrom""), dead or moved actors,\nand destinations a phase-3 actor now owns (fizzle);
  :a destination holding a ghost the snapshot lost is cleared,\nthen ""relocate"" with occupy trust — victim still home means\na single move-phase collision, never a second kill;
  :mirror the landing onto the phase-3 snapshot (move / blast /\ncollision, ""chaseFrom""-aware mine filter) → **afterMove** snapshot;
}

partition "Phase 4 — promotion" {
  :pawns that survived every phase promote on the ""afterAll"" board;
}
:return the four lists + the three snapshots;
note right
  **Shared with the UI replay:** ""applyPathRevealAttack"" /
  ""applyPathRevealCCShot"" are the single source of truth for the
  board-state fizzles; the loop above pre-filters the two engine-context
  gates (siege, re-occupied origin) so the UI only ever replays fired
  approaches. Neither helper clears mines — the walk-contact check owns that.

  **Do not "fix":** ""applyPendingCCShots"" gates firing on board occupancy
  and target identity only, never on the shooter's own HP. A king already at
  0 in the same pass still returns fire — that is what makes equal-HP contact
  end 0/0 as a draw instead of a win for whoever is ordered first.
end note
stop
@enduml
